    <selectionEntryGroup name="Miscellaneous" id="8672-4b89-a288-1774" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true">
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="aa88-fb8b-1a4a-f644" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="2"/>
      </constraints>
      <entryLinks>
        <entryLink name="Gnoblar Fighter" id="9410-910f-a32f-3993" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" targetId="79b7-5cfb-549c-c973" type="selectionEntry"/>
        <entryLink name="Luck Gnoblar" id="ec52-4569-3a0f-7faa" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" targetId="fb64-2749-b338-5d62" type="selectionEntry"/>
        <entryLink name="Lookout Gnoblar" id="4cb4-7182-602f-faba" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" targetId="4230-9ecf-d7b1-637e" type="selectionEntry"/>
        <entryLink name="Sword Gnoblar" id="d655-a211-ae59-7853" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" targetId="19a0-ec5f-4452-7e5b" type="selectionEntry"/>
      </entryLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Gnoblars" id="5fc0-8fb2-6f9c-ded2" hidden="false">
          <description>Ogres find simple pleasure in the bickering of Gnoblars and some claim one as their pet for amusement.
An astute Gnoblar puts his malice to good use and places the right action at the perfect moment to gain itself a master.

Treat these Gnoblars in all aspects like miscellaneous equipment (they are not models and do not occupy their own bases!).
However, if the Ogre owning them was taken out of action in a game, roll a D6 for each of his Gnoblars: on a 1-2 they are dead and removed from their master’s equipment.

Ogres may own up to two different Claimed Gnoblars.
These can be represented on the model they accompany.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
    <selectionEntryGroup name="Special Skills (Maneaters)" id="7228-d089-dfaf-7ef9" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true">
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="Master of Arms" id="0513-532c-f77d-3b51" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="be57-e54c-9114-9eb9" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0"/>
            <cost name="Warband Rating" typeId="wb-rating" value="0"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Master of Arms" id="55a8-7719-d99d-cd2b" hidden="false">
              <description>The Ogre learns how to use his size.
He may now wield a Difficult to Use weapon and a hand weapon at the same time, but not two Difficult to Use weapons.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Crude Belch" id="c196-b638-10d8-85f6" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="b108-aefe-c276-8661" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0"/>
            <cost name="Warband Rating" typeId="wb-rating" value="0"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Crude Belch" id="e50c-af19-f76b-0b26" hidden="false">
              <description>Ogres eat almost anything.
Consequences are to be expected from those inconsiderate enough to consume a rich meal before battle.
A Hero with this &apos;condition&apos; may unleash his thunderous fumes on all enemies engaged in close combat.
Those that do notpass a LeaDership test suffer a –1 ‘to hit’ modifier for the turn.
The Ogre must wait until a new enemy engages him incombat before he relieves himself again.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Bull Charge" id="85c9-2152-ff6e-8a68" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="5cc3-8833-356c-8dee" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0"/>
            <cost name="Warband Rating" typeId="wb-rating" value="0"/>
          </costs>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="02b5-2ebd-abd3-cf6a" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Bull Charge" id="45b3-15ce-e279-b417" hidden="false">
              <description>Ogres learn to use their vast bulk in a charge, trampling the enemy to the ground.
When charging, an Ogre with this skill may attempt a single attack with a +1 ‘to hit’ modifier rather than making his normal attacks.
If successful the enemy model is automatically knocked down.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Dog of War" id="76d1-b223-c318-4760" collective="false" hidden="true" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="f3dc-593b-1787-2024" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0"/>
            <cost name="Warband Rating" typeId="wb-rating" value="0"/>
          </costs>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="ea05-7e6b-115f-542a" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Dog of War" id="f8b5-ee82-ec91-f2a0" hidden="false">
              <description>When an Ogre travels south he can find employment as a tavern bouncer.
Some are enlisted by Paymasters to fight for Tilean City States.
Drawing from experience gained during a stint on foreign soil, the band can now hire those Hired Swords available for Mercenaries.
This skill may only be taken by the leader and if he dies all Hired Swords are removed from the warband.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Bellowing Roar" id="d84a-b946-a476-6e8b" collective="false" hidden="true" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="00a4-8406-bd96-eac3" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0"/>
            <cost name="Warband Rating" typeId="wb-rating" value="0"/>
          </costs>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="ea05-7e6b-115f-542a" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Bellowing Roar" id="ad9d-9da3-0156-7eec" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ogre leader expects challenges to his authority.
One of the best ways to suppress a mutineer in the ranks is to give his ear drums a good pounding.
This skill may only be taken by the warband leader, allowing him to re-roll the first failed Rout test.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Maneater" id="7e53-9a16-6955-c715" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="bab8-779c-c70e-df22" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
